{
  "abstract": "In a balanced stable-marriage market of size n, each participant independently chooses a uniformly random strict ranking. Write S_n for the number of stable complete matchings. For absolute constants C and t_0 greater than zero and every fixed 0 < t < t_0, the limit superior as n tends to infinity of Pr(S_n <= t n log n) is at most C t^2 log(e/t). Bo Cowgill and Will Cook are coauthors of this fixed-threshold result.",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "Bo Cowgill"
    }
  ],
